          "promptGuidance": "documentary reportage photograph, candid mid-distance vantage at standing eye level, available natural light, real working environment shown as it is, true-to-life neutral color with no tint or filter, one clear focal subject with honest depth, an uncluttered quiet area left for type, no posed people, no stock-photo smiles, no logos or readable signage",
          "subjects": "Real places where the deck's subject actually happens — a workplace, a street, a counter, a bench, a platform, a ward, a kitchen table — with the objects and moments that belong there. Never abstractions, generic desks, blank documents, handshakes, or idle hands.",
          "whenToUse": "Covers, act breaks, image-with-commentary splits, galleries, people cards, and evidence bands where a real scene grounds the words. Data never goes into a picture; charts and tables stay native."
